{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.u_multiset_available_at_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.u_multiset_available_at_identity","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L295-L302","doc":"**Quarks are exempt, and must be.**  The Borromean word `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³` has\nidentity permutation, so its three strands are three separate components and a\ncomponent framing may take a different value on each. `u = {0,1,1}` is therefore\navailable — as it must be, since a transitive π would have forced it constant\nand killed it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.e_framing_is_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.e_framing_is_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L285-L293","doc":"**e = {−1,−1,−1}, derived rather than enumerated.**  Same argument at\n`Q(e) = −1`: the battery's unique `e`-survivor is forced, not selected. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_distinct_multiset_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_distinct_multiset_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L269-L283","doc":"**`ν = {−1,0,1}` is excluded.**  A knot closure forces a constant framing,\nwhich is not injective on three strands — so the all-distinct survivor cannot be\n`ν`'s multiset.\n\nThis closes the half of `htw2`'s `1·2·2·1` residual that no total-only\ninvariant could reach: `Y`, the `ℤ₆` condition and bar-negation all see only the\ntotal, and both `ν`-survivors have total `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_framing_is_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_framing_is_zero","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L259-L267","doc":"**ν = {0,0,0}.**  `ν` is a lepton, so its closure is a knot (transitive π),\nand `Q(ν) = 0` gives total twist `0`. Hence every strand carries twist `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.lepton_framing_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.lepton_framing_determined","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L242-L257","doc":"**Lepton framing is determined**: transitive π forces constancy, and the\npinned total `3Q` then fixes the common value to `Q`.\n\nThis is the step that turns the `ν` ambiguity into a decision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.d_residual_not_separated_at_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.d_residual_not_separated_at_swap","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L206-L219","doc":"**The `d` residual is NOT separated — an honest negative.**\n\nBoth `d`-survivors have shape `(2,1)`, so at a `π` whose orbits are `{0,1}` and\n`{2}` *both* are realisable as component framings: `{−1,−1,1}` with the doubled\nvalue on the 2-orbit, and `{−1,0,0}` with the doubled value `0` there.\n\nComponent-constancy therefore cannot narrow `d`'s ambiguity. Separating it needs\nsomething finer than orbit shape — which *value* sits on which orbit — and that\nis not supplied by the framing condition alone. Recorded so this constraint is\nnot over-sold as closing the whole residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_residual_separated_at_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_residual_separated_at_swap","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L186-L204","doc":"**The `ν` residual IS separated.**\n\nIts two survivors have different shapes — `{−1,0,1}` is all-distinct, `{0,0,0}`\nis constant — so any `π ≠ 1` admits the second and forbids the first.\n\nStated at `π = swap 0 1`: the constant framing is component-compatible, while\n**no** component framing of that `π` is injective. Consequently, if `ν`'s\nclosure is not totally split, `ν = {0,0,0}` is forced and `{−1,0,1}` is\nexcluded — a constraint no total-only invariant can supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.const_isComponentFraming","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.const_isComponentFraming","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L180-L184","doc":"A constant framing is a component framing for **every** `π` — so the\nconstant survivors (`ν = {0,0,0}`, `e = {-1,-1,-1}`) are compatible with any\nbraid, and carry no constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_multiset_forces_trivial_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.nu_multiset_forces_trivial_perm","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L157-L163","doc":"`ν = {-1, 0, 1}` has pairwise-distinct entries, so `π = 1`: the closure is a\nthree-component split link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.u_multiset_forces_nontransitive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.u_multiset_forces_nontransitive","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L143-L155","doc":"`u = {0, 1, 1}` is not constant, so `u`'s braid closure is **not a knot**.\n\nHere the framing is exhibited concretely: strand 0 carries twist `0`, strands 1\nand 2 carry `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.eq_one_of_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.eq_one_of_injective","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L129-L136","doc":"**All-distinct twists force a totally split closure.**\n\nIf the framing is injective — the entries of the multiset are pairwise distinct —\nthen `π` is the identity, so the closure is an `n`-component split link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.constant_of_transitive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.constant_of_transitive","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L112-L127","doc":"**A knot closure forces a constant framing.**\n\nIf `π` is transitive — every strand reachable from every other, i.e. the closure\nhas a single component — then a component framing takes one value throughout, so\nits multiset is `{a, …, a}`.\n\nContrapositive, which is the usable form: a **non-constant** multiset proves the\nclosure is *not* a knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.invariant_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.invariant_pow","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L100-L110","doc":"Invariance under `π` propagates to every power of `π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.IsComponentFraming","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ComponentFraming.IsComponentFraming","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ComponentFraming.lean#L92-L98","doc":"A **component framing**: a per-strand integer that is constant along the\nclosure, i.e. invariant under the braid's underlying permutation.\n\nStrands `i` and `π i` are joined by the closure, so they lie on one component of\nthe resulting link; a framing of that link assigns them the same integer. ","signatureChunk":0}]}